IMPORT prelude

-- Merchant Shipping (Maritime Labour Convention) Act 2014 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a seafarer on a Singapore ship and
-- for the shipowner who employs one: minimum ages and young seafarers (ss 2, 5, 6, 17, 18, 19), medical fitness certificates (ss 7,
-- 8, 9), notice to end the employment agreement (s 14), hours of rest (s 16), late wages (s 20), annual leave (s 22), repatriation
-- (s 23), wages after a wreck or sale (s 24), and the shipowner's liability for sickness and injury (ss 35, 36, 38, 39), with a few
-- maximum fines (ss 5, 12, 16, 34).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MSMLCA2014.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates
-- all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amending Act
-- annotated in the body is 16/2020 (piracy and captivity, ss 14(13), 20(8), 23(2)(e), 34(4)). SSO retrieval 3 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0107 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the employment terms a seafarer or shipowner meets. Not encoded: application and exemption (ss 3, 4) beyond
-- the definitions used, recruitment-service regulation beyond the fee ban (s 12), crew lists (s 15), wage accounts and allotments
-- (ss 20(4)-(7), 21), catering (Part 5), on-board medical provision (ss 28-33), financial security and its providers (ss 34, 34A)
-- beyond the penalty, health and safety (Part 7), certification and inspection (Parts 8 to 10), complaints (Part 9), and the
-- miscellaneous Part 11. Nothing in the Convention itself or in regulations was read.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Merchant Shipping (Maritime Labour Convention) Act 2014 -- seafarers`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` a b MEANS IF a GREATER THAN b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `2, 5, 6 -- ages`

-- s 2(1): "'young seafarer' means any seafarer who is 16 years of age or above and below 18 years of age".
-- s 5(1): "A person must not cause or permit a person below 16 years of age to be employed on board a ship"; (2) fine up to $5,000.
-- s 6(1): "A seafarer below 18 years of age must not be employed or engaged, or work, as a ship's cook"; (2) fine up to $5,000.
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seafarer is a young seafarer` IF
    `the age` AT LEAST 16 AND `the age` LESS THAN 18

GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employing the person on board is an offence under section 5` IF
    `the age` LESS THAN 16

GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seafarer may work as a ship's cook` IF
    `the age` AT LEAST 18

§§ `19 -- hazardous work`

-- s 19(1): "A person must not cause or permit any young seafarer to be employed in any hazardous work on any ship"; (2) $10,000.
-- (3): the list -- heavy loads; entry into boilers, tanks and cofferdams; harmful noise and vibration; hoisting and power machinery;
-- mooring or tow lines or ground tackle; "rigging"; work aloft or on deck in heavy weather; electrical equipment; harmful materials;
-- "cleaning of catering machinery"; ship's boats. The list is closed ("means any of the following work").
DECLARE Work IS ONE OF
    `rigging`
    `cleaning of catering machinery`
    `entry into a cargo tank`
    `serving meals in the mess`

GIVEN `the work` IS A Work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work is hazardous work` IF
    CONSIDER `the work`
    WHEN `serving meals in the mess` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `7, 8, 9 -- medical fitness certificates`

-- s 9: valid from the examination and for the period on it, not exceeding "(a) in respect of a person below 18 years of age, one
-- year; (b) in respect of a person of 18 years of age or above, 2 years".
GIVEN `the age at examination` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest validity in years` MEANS
    IF `the age at examination` LESS THAN 18 THEN 1 ELSE 2

-- s 7(3), 8(2): a certificate expiring "during the course of a voyage" -- the seafarer may continue to work until the earlier of
-- "(a) the first port of call at which it is possible ... to be examined" and "(b) the end of 3 months starting from the date of the
-- expiry". (Months are counted as whole months here.)
GIVEN `months since expiry` IS A NUMBER, `reached a port where examination is possible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seafarer may keep working on the expired certificate` IF
    (NOT `reached a port where examination is possible`) AND `months since expiry` LESS THAN 3

-- s 7(4), 8(3): "In urgent cases, with the Director's approval", a person without a valid certificate who "has held a medical
-- fitness certificate for at least 24 months (or in the case of a person below 18 years of age at the date of issue of the
-- certificate, at least 12 months)" which "expired no earlier than one month before" joining may work until the first port where
-- examination is possible, "but in any case not for a period exceeding 3 months".
GIVEN `under 18 at issue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months the old certificate must have been held` MEANS
    IF `under 18 at issue` THEN 12 ELSE 24

GIVEN `the Director approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `months held` IS A NUMBER, `under 18 at issue` IS A BOOLEAN, `months from expiry to joining` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the urgent-case exception applies` IF
        `the Director approved`
    AND `months held` AT LEAST `the months the old certificate must have been held` `under 18 at issue`
    AND `months from expiry to joining` AT MOST 1

§§ `14 -- ending the employment agreement`

-- s 14(10): notice "must be the same for both the shipowner and the seafarer ... provided that the notice period is not less than
-- 7 days, except in circumstances prescribed under subsection (14)(c)". (11): written; "the day on which the notice is given must be
-- included in the period of the notice". (12): either party may end it at once by paying the gross rate of pay for the notice period.
GIVEN `notice days` IS A NUMBER, `a prescribed shorter period applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice period is long enough` IF
    `notice days` AT LEAST 7 OR `a prescribed shorter period applies`

GIVEN `day the notice is given` IS A NUMBER, `notice days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of the notice` MEANS
    `day the notice is given` PLUS `notice days` MINUS 1

§§ `16 -- hours of rest`

-- s 16(2): "The minimum hours of rest are 10 hours in any 24-hour period and 77 hours in any 7-day period." (3): divided "into no
-- more than 2 periods, one of which must be at least 6 hours in length, and the interval between consecutive periods of rest must
-- not exceed 14 hours". (5): no payment in lieu. (9), (10): Director's exceptions and emergencies, not modelled. (11): a shipowner who
-- contravenes (1) -- fine up to $10,000.
DECLARE RestRecord HAS
    `hours of rest in the 24-hour period` IS A NUMBER
    `hours of rest in the 7-day period` IS A NUMBER
    `number of rest periods` IS A NUMBER
    `longest rest period` IS A NUMBER
    `longest interval between rest periods` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the record` IS A RestRecord
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hours of rest comply` IF
        `the record`'s `hours of rest in the 24-hour period` AT LEAST 10
    AND `the record`'s `hours of rest in the 7-day period` AT LEAST 77
    AND `the record`'s `number of rest periods` AT MOST 2
    AND `the record`'s `longest rest period` AT LEAST 6
    AND `the record`'s `longest interval between rest periods` AT MOST 14

§§ `17, 18 -- young seafarers' hours and night work`

-- s 17(1)(a): "a person must not require any young seafarer to work more than 8 hours per day or 40 hours per week"; (2) unless the
-- master is of the opinion that training "would be impaired" or the limits are impracticable for watchkeeping or rostered shift work.
-- s 17 carries no penalty of its own.
GIVEN `hours per day` IS A NUMBER, `hours per week` IS A NUMBER, `the master's training or watchkeeping opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the young seafarer's hours are permitted` IF
    `the master's training or watchkeeping opinion` OR (`hours per day` AT MOST 8 AND `hours per week` AT MOST 40)

-- s 18(1): no young seafarer "in any kind of night work"; (2) unless the Director approves; (3) $10,000; (4) "'night work' means work
-- done between 9 p.m. and 6 a.m. of the following day according to the time zone the ship is in". (The hour is a clock hour 0-23.)
GIVEN `the hour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hour is night work` IF
    `the hour` AT LEAST 21 OR `the hour` LESS THAN 6

GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER, `the hour` IS A NUMBER, `the Director approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the night work is an offence under section 18` IF
    `the seafarer is a young seafarer` `the age` AND `the hour is night work` `the hour` AND (NOT `the Director approved`)

§§ `20 -- late wages`

-- s 20(1): wages paid "in full on a monthly basis, before the expiry of the last day of the month". (2): if not paid, "the seafarer
-- is entitled to wages at the rate last payable ... for every day on which the amount remains unpaid until it is paid in full".
-- (3): not where the failure "was due to any reasonable dispute as to liability or to the act or default of the seafarer or to any
-- other cause, not being the wrongful act or default" of the payer.
GIVEN `daily rate` IS A NUMBER, `days unpaid` IS A NUMBER, `the delay is excused by subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the extra wages for late payment` MEANS
    IF `the delay is excused by subsection (3)` THEN 0 ELSE `daily rate` TIMES `days unpaid`

§§ `22 -- annual leave`

-- s 22(1): paid annual leave "of at least 2.5 days per month of continuous service". (3): shorter than 12 months, "annual leave in
-- proportion to the number of completed months". (11): "any fraction of a day which is less than one-half of a day is disregarded and
-- where the fraction of the day is one-half or more it is regarded as one day".
GIVEN `completed months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the annual leave in days` MEANS
    FLOOR (`completed months` TIMES 2.5 PLUS 0.5)

-- s 22(9): leave must be granted and taken "not later than 12 months after the end of every 12 months of continuous service and any
-- seafarer who fails to take that leave by the end of such period ceases to be entitled to the leave".
GIVEN `months after the service year ended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `untaken leave is lost` IF
    `months after the service year ended` GREATER THAN 12

§§ `23 -- repatriation`

-- s 23(2): the shipowner "must repatriate" where (a) the agreement "has expired"; (b) it "has been terminated by the seafarer for
-- justified reasons or by the shipowner"; (c) the seafarer cannot carry out duties -- illness, shipwreck, insolvency or sale, "the
-- ship is bound for a war zone ... to which the seafarer does not consent to go", industrial award, left behind; (d) abandonment,
-- including failure "to pay the seafarer's contractual wages for a period of at least 2 months"; (e) release from captivity after
-- piracy or armed robbery.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `the agreement has expired`
    `the shipowner ended the agreement`
    `the seafarer ended it for justified reasons`
    `the seafarer ended it without justified reasons`
    `shipwreck`
    `the ship is bound for a war zone the seafarer refuses`
    `release from captivity after piracy`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shipowner must repatriate` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the seafarer ended it without justified reasons` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `months of wages unpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unpaid wages require repatriation` IF
    `months of wages unpaid` AT LEAST 2

§§ `24 -- wreck, loss or sale of the ship`

-- s 24(1), (2): a seafarer whose employment ends early because the ship is wrecked, lost, sold or leaves the register is "entitled
-- to wages, at the rate payable under the agreement ... for every day on which he or she is unemployed in the 2 months following".
-- (3): not for a day on which the seafarer "was able to obtain suitable employment ... but unreasonably refused to take it".
GIVEN `daily rate` IS A NUMBER, `days unemployed in the 2 months` IS A NUMBER, `days suitable work was unreasonably refused` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the wreck wages` MEANS
    `daily rate` TIMES (`days unemployed in the 2 months` MINUS `days suitable work was unreasonably refused`)

§§ `35, 36, 38 -- sickness and injury`

-- s 35(1): the shipowner meets expenses "reasonably incurred in connection with a seafarer's sickness or injury" which first occurs
-- between the start of the agreement and the end of the duty to repatriate, or later but "caused by circumstances or events arising
-- during that period". s 36 is the matching duty to make up wages.
-- s 38: neither applies where "(a) the injury ... was incurred otherwise than in the service of the ship; (b) ... due to the
-- seafarer's wilful misconduct; or (c) the sickness or incapacity for work existed on the date on which the seafarer entered the
-- seafarer's employment agreement, and the seafarer deliberately concealed" it.
DECLARE Harm HAS
    `first occurred in the covered period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by events in the covered period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `incurred in the service of the ship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `due to wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `existed at signing and was deliberately concealed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shipowner is liable under sections 35 and 36` IF
        (`the harm`'s `first occurred in the covered period` OR `the harm`'s `caused by events in the covered period`)
    AND `the harm`'s `incurred in the service of the ship`
    AND (NOT `the harm`'s `due to wilful misconduct`)
    AND (NOT `the harm`'s `existed at signing and was deliberately concealed`)

-- s 35(4): limited to expenses incurred from the date the sickness or injury first occurs "ending on the expiry of 16 weeks after that
-- date" -- counted here as 112 days after the onset date.
GIVEN `days after onset` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the expense falls in the 16 weeks` IF
    `days after onset` AT MOST 112

-- s 39(1): compensation under s 35 "must be reduced by the amount" already received for medical treatment under the Work Injury
-- Compensation Act 2019; (3)(b) "a seafarer must not be compensated more than once in respect of the same expense".
GIVEN `expenses` IS A NUMBER, `WICA medical compensation received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the medical expenses still recoverable` MEANS
    `the larger of` (`expenses` MINUS `WICA medical compensation received`) 0

-- s 36(2): the shipowner pays the difference between "any wages received" and "the full wages which would have been payable" had the
-- seafarer remained fit; (6) recoverable "as a civil debt".
GIVEN `full wages` IS A NUMBER, `wages received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the wage top-up` MEANS
    `the larger of` (`full wages` MINUS `wages received`) 0

§§ `5, 12, 16, 34 -- some maximum fines`

-- s 5(2): $5,000. s 12(1), (2): operating an unauthorised recruitment and placement service, or demanding or receiving "any
-- remuneration for providing the prospective employee with employment" -- $5,000 or 2 years or both. s 16(11): $10,000.
-- s 34(5): letting a ship go to sea without the required insurance or financial security -- $10,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `employing a person under 16 on board`
    `charging a seafarer for a job`
    `not giving the hours of rest`
    `sailing without financial security`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `employing a person under 16 on board` THEN 5000
    WHEN `charging a seafarer for a job` THEN 5000
    WHEN `not giving the hours of rest` THEN 10000
    WHEN `sailing without financial security` THEN 10000
